    a: "A loan is in balance when the undrawn loan plus equity still to come covers the cost to finish. If an overrun pushes the cost to complete above that, the loan is out of balance and the lender stops funding until the sponsor deposits the shortfall. Because the lender's money goes in last, overruns fall on the sponsor first.",
