    q: "How do you work out the most you can pay for a development site?",
    a: "Work backward from the finished project. Value the stabilized building (NOI ÷ exit cap), take off the profit you need, then subtract every non-land cost: hard, soft, financing and contingency. What's left is the residual land value, the most you can pay and still hit your return. If the seller wants more, the project doesn't work at that price.",
